Title: Upstream tsconfig excludes tests, so typecheck never covers the suite
Created: 2026-09-01
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-01T09:40Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Found by the 0091 takeover session during the PR A/B merge, reported
2026-09-01: upstream's `tsconfig.json` excludes `tests`, so `npm run
typecheck` never typechecks the test suite. A test importing a symbol that no
longer exists passes typecheck and fails only at runtime — it bit during the
merge of the two prepared droplist branches, where a rename (`HighDf` →
`Prunable`) left a test compiling against a ghost.

The defect class is the familiar one: a gate whose all-clear is
indistinguishable from not looking. Upstream's own contribution bar asks for
`npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test` green; the first of the three
silently covers only half the tree.

## Relevant files
- Upstream `tsconfig.json` — the `exclude` entry.
- Upstream `package.json` — the `typecheck` script.

## Actions
1. Verify at current upstream HEAD that the exclusion is still present and
   that a deliberately broken test import passes `npm run typecheck` (the
   positive control — do not trust the report without it).
2. Measure the blast radius: run `tsc --noEmit` over the suite once; the
   exclusion may be hiding accumulated type errors in tests, which changes
   the fix from one line to a cleanup.
3. Decide the upstream form per the measured asymmetry: a one-line fix with a
   clean suite is a contained PR; an exclusion hiding many latent errors is
   design-sized enough to go as an issue he fixes his own way.

## Test
- The positive control in action 1 is the red step: a test file importing a
  nonexistent symbol must fail typecheck after the fix and pass before it.

## Verification
- [ ] Positive control demonstrated both sides of the fix
- [ ] Blast radius measured and recorded here

## Invariants
- GOVERNANCE.md bounds apply to any filing; nothing goes upstream without
  the author's authorization.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Filed upstream (form per action 3) or an explicit deliberately-unfiled
      line recorded here, per GOVERNANCE.md § The courtesy filing
- [ ] Outcome recorded in SYNC.md's tracker
